      ],
      "description": "Offline gfx950/CDNA4 ISA reference -- the WHOLE 608-page ISA document is transcribed into three committed databases, so on gfx950 never render or fetch the PDF and never assert a hardware fact from memory. No network, no GPU, no PDF. START WITH `search <term>`: it queries all three at once. `layout`/`locate`/`facts`/`modifiers`/`sparse` = MFMA operand layout, lane/VGPR/byte for A,B,C,D (ch.7). `opcodes`/`encoding`/`format` = all 1240 instructions and 33 encodings plus their pseudo-code (ch.12-13). `regs`/`waitcnt`/`waits`/`hazard`/`lds`/`mem`/`limits`/`concepts`/`tables` = registers, wait states and manual NOPs, LDS and memory model, programming limits (ch.1-6, 8-11). `errata` = known errors in the printed document -- read it before hand-assembling or trusting a printed opcode. Every answer prints a `# provenance:` line with the ISA page to cite."
    },
