      "description": "AMD hardware primary sources, tiered (references/hardware/primary-sources.md). START WITH `preflight`: it prints which architecture x question class is answerable in THIS environment and the exact repair command for anything that is not -- run it before you need an answer, not when a lever already failed. `layout <arch> <instr>` generates the operand layout table: for cdna1/2/3 and rdna3/4 from the AMD Matrix Instruction Calculator, for gfx950 from the in-pack ISA database (the calculator has no cdna4 support, which is why that arch ships one). `xml <arch>` fetches the machine-readable ISA XML; `decode <arch> <bytes>` disassembles raw encoding bytes; `pdf <doc> [p0 p1]` renders pages for prose no database carries. Tiers that fetch need TILE_HW_CACHE; preflight, --help and every in-pack database do not."
    },
